; DRC debug-marker fixture (compile-and-assert; also bootable).
;
; DRC's backend has a "fake" condact, FAKE_DEBUG_CONDACT_CODE = 220 =
; $DC (drb.php:18), which an author gets by writing DEBUG in the source.
; DRB DROPS it unless the game is compiled with the -D flag, and -D is
; only legal for target ZX/CPC (drb.php:1764); with -D it goes into the
; process tables VERBATIM, opcode byte and NOTHING ELSE - it is a
; breakpoint marker for the ZEsarUX DAAD debugger ("k: Set a breakpoint
; fired with a special Daad condact"), not something an interpreter is
; meant to perform.
;
; $DC & $7F is 92 = NEWTEXT, so an interpreter that strips the
; indirection bit before dispatching runs a NEWTEXT at every marker -
; discarding the player's pending compound order and stamping the table
; done. tests\build-tests.ps1 compiles this file TWICE, with and without
; DRB's -d, and asserts both DDBs byte for byte.
;
; This is deliberately the smallest thing that carries all three facts:
;   PRO 1  DEBUG / ISNDONE / MESSAGE - the marker must not mark the
;          table done, which is what the dispatcher's pre-dispatch
;          Action stamp would do if $DC reached the condact table;
;   PRO 2  DEBUG / NEWTEXT / DEBUG - the marker's $DC and a REAL
;          NEWTEXT's $5C adjacent in one stream, which is the whole
;          ambiguity question settled in bytes (DRB only sets the
;          indirection bit on a condact that HAS parameters,
;          drb.php:1130, and NEWTEXT has none - so a real NEWTEXT can
;          never encode as $DC). PRO 2 is never called: only PRO 0 runs
;          by itself and nothing does PROCESS 2.
;   sizes  three DEBUG lines cost exactly three DDB bytes, which is the
;          marker's zero-parameter arity proved rather than assumed.
;
; OWNER LEG (optional - the host assertions above are complete on their
; own): copy tests\out\debugflag-debug.ddb into any staged sd\<LEG>\
; folder as GAME.DDB and boot it. Expect
;   DBG MARKER FIXTURE
;   PASS - marker invisible
; An interpreter that performs the marker prints "FAIL - marker acted as
; NEWTEXT" instead, because the marker's Action stamp fails the ISNDONE.
; tests\out\debugflag.ddb (no -d) is the control and must print PASS on
; any build at all - the markers are not in it.
/CTL
_
/VOC
NORTH  2  noun
/STX
/0  "It's too dark to see anything."
/1  "I can also see:"
/2  "What now?"
/3  "What next?"
/4  "What should I do now?"
/5  "What should I do next?"
/6  "I didn't understand."
/7  "I can't go in that direction."
/8  "I can't do that."
/9  "I have with me:"
/10 "I am wearing:"
/11 " "
/12 "Are you sure?"
/13 "Another go?"
/14 " "
/15 "OK."
/16 "Press any key."
/17 " "
/18 " "
/19 " "
/20 " "
/21 " "
/22 " "
/23 "I'm not wearing one of those."
/24 "I can't. My hands are full."
/25 "I already have the _."
/26 "There isn't one of those here."
/27 "I can't carry any more things."
/28 "I don't have one of those."
/29 "I'm already wearing the _."
/30 "Y"
/31 "N"
/32 "More..."
/33 ">"
/34 " "
/35 " "
/36 "I now have the _."
/37 "I'm now wearing the _."
/38 "I've removed the _."
/39 "I've dropped the _."
/40 "I can't wear the _."
/41 "I can't remove the _."
/42 "I can't remove the _. My hands are full."
/43 "The _ weighs too much for me."
/44 "The _ is in the"
/45 "The _ isn't in the"
/46 ", "
/47 " and "
/48 ".#n"
/49 "I don't have the _."
/50 "I'm not wearing the _."
/51 "."
/52 "There isn't one of those in the"
/53 "Nothing."
/54 " "
/55 " "
/56 " "
/57 "I/O Error"
/58 " "
/59 "File name error."
/60 "Type in name of file."
/MTX
/0 "DBG MARKER FIXTURE#n"
/1 "PASS - marker invisible#n"
/2 "FAIL - marker acted as NEWTEXT#n"
/OTX
/0 "a thing"
/LTX
/0 "Arena."
/CON
/0
/OBJ
/0    0   1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   NORTH _
/PRO 0
> _ _   CLS
        MESSAGE 0
        PROCESS 1
/PRO 1
> _ _   DEBUG
        ISNDONE
        MESSAGE 1
        DONE
> _ _   MESSAGE 2
        DONE
/PRO 2
> _ _   DEBUG
        NEWTEXT
        DEBUG
/END
